cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PULSAR — Python characterization suite for neural-stimulation electrodes"
message: "If you use PULSAR in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Christopher K.
    # ORCID / affiliation can be added here when available.
abstract: >
  PULSAR is a PyQt6 desktop application for characterizing neural-
  stimulation microelectrode arrays.  It drives a Plexon PlexStim 2.0
  stimulator and a Tektronix TBS-series oscilloscope through a
  guided experimental workflow: voltage-transient sweeps, progressive
  stress staircases, short pulsing, and long pulsing.  Live metrics
  cover Shannon k-value, injected charge (Q_inj), driving voltage
  (V_d), access voltage (V_a), access resistance (R_a), polarization
  potential (E_pol), double-layer capacitance (C_d), and interpulse
  potential.  A companion viewer (POLARIS) renders saved sessions
  with channel-mapped metric tables, multi-channel overlays, and
  Q_inj vs. amplitude / V_d vs. Q_inj analysis plots.
keywords:
  - neural stimulation
  - microelectrode characterization
  - voltage transient
  - charge injection
  - Plexon PlexStim
  - Tektronix oscilloscope
  - electrophysiology
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bortz1234/StimulationTesting"
url: "https://github.com/Bortz1234/StimulationTesting"
version: 0.2.0
